# Model Rules

## Structure
```python
from __future__ import annotations

from django.db import models
from django.utils.translation import gettext_lazy as _


class MyModel(models.Model):
    """One-line description of the model."""

    name = models.CharField(_("name"), max_length=255)
    created_at = models.DateTimeField(auto_now_add=True)
    updated_at = models.DateTimeField(auto_now=True)

    class Meta:
        ordering = ["-created_at"]
        verbose_name = _("my model")
        verbose_name_plural = _("my models")

    def __str__(self) -> str:
        return self.name
```

## Rules
- Always define `__str__`
- Always define `Meta` with `verbose_name` and `verbose_name_plural`
- Use `gettext_lazy` for all field `verbose_name` and `help_text`
- Use `created_at` / `updated_at` on every model
- After any model change: run `uv run python src/manage.py makemigrations`
